<title>USA: USDA raises Russia GSM-102 credit line by $25 mln.</title>
<headline>USDA raises Russia GSM-102 credit line by $25 mln.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Agriculture Department Tuesday said it raised Russia's GSM-102 credit guarantee line by $25 million to a total of $120 million for fiscal year 1997.</p>
<p>USDA said all other terms and conditions remain the same.</p>
<p>The commodities covered include cotton, animal feed products, breeder livestock, dairy products, feedgrains, oilseeds, meat, wheat and vegetable oil.</p>
